A shared harness already exists at translation/tests/common/mod.rs. Read it first. Use it like this:

```rust
mod common;
use common::*;
use std::os::raw::{c_int, c_uint, c_void};

// fnpair! returns (c_fn, rust_fn) for the same symbol from both .so files
type FnFoo = unsafe extern "C" fn(*mut c_void, size_t) -> size_t;
let (cf, rf) = fnpair!("FSE_compress", FnFoo);
```

The harness provides: `size_t`, `Rng` (seeded xorshift: `Rng::new(seed)`, `.next_u32()`, `.next_u64()`, `.below(n)`, `.range(lo,hi)`), `Shape` enum + `ALL_SHAPES` + `gen(shape, len, &mut rng) -> Vec<u8>`, `assert_bytes_eq(ctx, &c, &r)`, `FnIsError`, `FnErrName`, `FnSizeSize`, `cstr()`, and constants. It also has `pair::<T>(name)` if you need a data symbol.

What to test (read c_src/src/common/fse.h, c_src/src/common/huf.h, c_src/src/compress/hist.h, c_src/src/common/xxhash.h for exact signatures — note XXH_NAMESPACE=ZSTD_ so xxhash symbols are named ZSTD_XXH32, ZSTD_XXH64, ZSTD_XXH64_createState, ZSTD_XXH64_reset, ZSTD_XXH64_update, ZSTD_XXH64_digest, ZSTD_XXH32_canonicalFromHash, ZSTD_XXH64_hashFromCanonical, etc. Confirm the actual exported names with: nm -D --defined-only c_src/build/libzstd.so | grep -E ' T ' | grep -E 'FSE_|HUF_|HIST_|XXH'):

1. FSE: FSE_compress, FSE_compress2 (across all valid maxSymbolValue/tableLog combos), FSE_decompress, FSE_compressBound, FSE_isError, FSE_getErrorName, FSE_optimalTableLog, FSE_normalizeCount, FSE_writeNCount, FSE_readNCount, FSE_readNCount_bmi2, FSE_buildCTable*/FSE_buildDTable*, FSE_compress_usingCTable, FSE_decompress_usingDTable, FSE_createCTable/freeCTable/createDTable/freeDTable, FSE_compress_wksp, FSE_decompress_wksp, FSE_decompress_wksp_bmi2. Compare returned sizes AND output bytes AND, for the table-building functions, the full contents of the produced CTable/DTable/normalizedCounter arrays byte-for-byte.
2. HUF: HUF_compress, HUF_compress2, HUF_compress4X_wksp, HUF_compress4X_repeat, HUF_compress1X_wksp, HUF_compress1X_repeat, HUF_compressBound, HUF_decompress, HUF_decompress1X1/1X2/4X1/4X2 and their _DCtx / _usingDTable / _wksp / _bmi2 variants, HUF_readStats, HUF_readStats_wksp, HUF_readDTableX1/X2 (and _wksp), HUF_writeCTable*, HUF_buildCTable*, HUF_estimateCompressedSize, HUF_validateCTable, HUF_getNbBitsFromCTable, HUF_optimalTableLog, HUF_getErrorName, HUF_isError, HUF_decompress4X_hufOnly*. Compare sizes, bytes, and the produced CTable/DTable memory.
3. HIST: HIST_count, HIST_count_simple, HIST_count_wksp, HIST_countFast, HIST_countFast_wksp, HIST_isError. Compare the whole count[] array and the return value.
4. xxhash: ZSTD_XXH32/ZSTD_XXH64 one-shot over many lengths (0..300 plus large), all seed values from a seeded Rng, plus the streaming API (createState/reset/update in randomized chunk splits/digest/freeState) and canonical conversions. Also ZSTD_XXH32_copyState / ZSTD_XXH64_copyState if exported.

Requirements:
- Use MANY randomized inputs per case with a FIXED seed, driven by `Rng`. Use all of `ALL_SHAPES` and many length classes including 0, 1, 2, 3, and around 128/255/256/512/64KB/128KB boundaries.
- For every call, compare the return value exactly, and when it is not an error, compare the full output buffer bytes. When it IS an error, compare that both sides report error via the matching FSE_isError/HUF_isError AND compare the error name string.
- Give every assertion a descriptive context string including the shape/length/params so failures are diagnosable.
- Group tests into several #[test] functions so failures localize.
- Zero-init all output buffers to the SAME pattern (e.g. 0xAA) on both sides before each call, and compare the FULL buffer including the untouched tail where the C semantics make that meaningful (for table buffers, compare the whole table).
- Use `unsafe` blocks; never call Rust functions directly, only through the fnpair! symbols.

