1. ZDICT_trainFromBuffer — many randomized sample sets. IMPORTANT: dictionary training needs many samples of real-ish redundant data; build sample buffers by concatenating many overlapping text-like/repetitive chunks (use Shape::Text, Shape::Repetitive, Shape::Mixed, Shape::LongRange) with a samplesSizes array. Vary: number of samples (small like 5-10 up to a few hundred), sample sizes (uniform and highly skewed), and requested dictBufferCapacity (small, exact, generous). Compare the returned size AND, when not an error, the ENTIRE produced dictionary buffer byte-for-byte.
