[38;5;252m[1m## The one real bug found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mZSTD_compressStream_generic[0m in [38;5;10msrc/compress/zstd_compress_frame.rs[0m. The C state machine is a [38;5;10mswitch[0m inside a [38;5;10mwhile (someMoreWork)[0m loop, where a bare [38;5;10mbreak;[0m exits the [3mswitch[23m and lets the loop iterate to the next block. The Rust translation used a [38;5;10mmatch[0m inside a [38;5;10mwhile[0m, where [38;5;10mbreak[0m exits the [3mloop[23m. Streaming compression therefore returned after a single block instead of consuming as much input as the C does.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Symptoms: with a 140 KB input and [38;5;10mZSTD_e_continue[0m, C consumed 140000 bytes while Rust stopped at 131072 (one [38;5;10mZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX[0m); step-count traces diverged on multi-block inputs with small output buffers. Fixed by wrapping the [38;5;10mmatch[0m in a labelled block so [38;5;10mbreak 'sw[0m reproduces C's switch-break semantics (12 sites). I then scanned the rest of the crate for the same mistranslation pattern — the decompression state machine already used [38;5;10mcontinue[0m correctly, and the other hits were false positives on the [38;5;10mr#match[0m variable name.[0m[0m
